        "finding": "Trigger is the actual held activation/deactivation special melee sweep hit. Normal, special-active follow-up, and pushfollow actions may benefit while active but do not trigger; pure push is excluded. Counter refreshes to 4, qualifying sweep finish normally leaves 3, then each held active finish consumes one including a miss; multi-spline/multi-target does not multiply the decrement. The page distinguishes no retroactive trigger-hit damage, later hit in a still-open sweep after cache refresh, switch gate, and no TTL/stacking."
      },
      {
        "area": "Power consumers and calculation",
        "result": "PASS",
        "finding": "Actual melee_power_level_modifier affects damage and impact power distribution and the cleave budget path. Documentation describes increased power inputs and explicitly avoids promising the same percentage in final health damage, stagger result, or hit count. The S formula and q additive example are scoped to already scaled power input; q=.20 plus tier-IV .30 yields 1.50, not multiplicative 1.56."
      },
      {
        "area": "Cleave budget timing",
